---
import Layout from '@layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="How to Use Didi in China as a Foreigner" lang="en">
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto py-12">
    <header class="mb-10">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-gray-500 mb-4">
        <a href="/en/transport/" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline">Transport</a>
        <span>&rarr;</span>
        <span>Tutorial</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900 leading-tight mb-4">
        How to Use Didi in China as a Foreigner
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-gray-500">
        Set up and use Didi (China's Uber) without a Chinese phone number. Ride options, payment, and tips.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose prose-gray max-w-none">
      <p>Didi is the Uber of China &#8212; and it's even more dominant here than Uber ever was in the US. Practically everyone uses it, and as a traveler, it will be your best friend for door-to-door trips.</p>

      <p>Good news: you can use Didi without a Chinese phone number. Here's how.</p>

      <h2>Method 1: Use Didi Through Alipay (Easiest)</h2>
      <p>If you already have Alipay set up (and you should &#8212; see the <a href="/en/payment/setup-alipay/">Alipay setup guide</a>):</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Open Alipay</li>
        <li>Scroll down to "Mini Programs" (or search for "Didi")</li>
        <li>Tap the Didi mini-program</li>
        <li>Allow location access</li>
        <li>You're in. Set your pickup and destination, choose a ride type, and confirm.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>Payment goes through Alipay automatically. No Chinese phone number needed.</p>

      <h2>Method 2: Download the Didi App</h2>
      <p>The Didi app has an English version. Download it from your app store (search "Didi Rider"). You can register with an international phone number, and the interface can be switched to English in settings.</p>
      <p>Payment methods supported: Alipay, WeChat Pay, Visa/Mastercard (add in-app).</p>

      <h2>Ride Types</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Express (&#24555;&#36710;):</strong> Standard ride, cheapest option. Comparable to UberX.</li>
        <li><strong>Premier (&#20248;&#20139;):</strong> Slightly nicer cars, a bit more expensive.</li>
        <li><strong>Taxi (&#20986;&#31199;&#36710;):</strong> Hails a regular taxi through the app. You pay the meter rate digitally.</li>
        <li><strong>Luxury (&#35946;&#21326;&#36710;):</strong> High-end cars (Mercedes, BMW). Expensive.</li>
        <li><strong>Hiring a Car (&#21253;&#36710;):</strong> Book a driver for multiple hours or a full day.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Tips for Using Didi</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Set your pickup accurately:</strong> Drag the pin on the map to exactly where you're standing. Drivers often can't find you if the pin is off.</li>
        <li><strong>Check the license plate:</strong> Match the plate number in the app to the car. Safety is generally good, but be smart.</li>
        <li><strong>Use the in-app chat:</strong> If your driver can't find you, the app has a built-in translation feature for chatting.</li>
        <li><strong>Be patient with pickup:</strong> In busy areas, your driver might be a few minutes away.</li>
        <li><strong>Tolls and fees:</strong> Highway tolls and airport parking fees are added to your fare automatically.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What About Uber?</h2>
      <p>Uber sold its China operations to Didi in 2016. The Uber app still works in China but only for international travelers (riders), and driver availability is limited. Didi is the default ride-hailing service &#8212; you'll get faster pickups and better coverage.</p>

      <p class="mt-8 p-4 bg-brand-50 rounded-xl">
        <strong>Summary:</strong> Use Didi through Alipay &#8212; no extra app, no Chinese phone number, payment handled automatically. It's the most convenient way to get around.
      </p>

      <p><a href="/en/transport/transport-guide/">&larr; Back to the complete transport guide</a></p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
